    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale hotel project in Mexico**, owners and developers commonly shortlist a mix of **Mexican upper-upscale brands** and **international upscale/luxury brands** that already have a visible presence in the market.[1][4][11][16]\n\nThe brands most clearly supported by the search results are:\n\n- **Camino Real** and **Quinta Real** from Grupo Camino Real, with **Camino Real** explicitly positioned as *upscale* and **Quinta Real** as *luxury*.[1]\n- **Fiesta Americana** and **Live Aqua** from Grupo Posadas, with **Fiesta Americana** described as *upscale* and **Live Aqua** as *ultra-luxury*.[3][11]\n- **JW Marriott**, **Marriott**, and **Four Points by Sheraton** from Marriott’s Mexico portfolio; **JW Marriott** appears in Mexico’s luxury lodging inventory and Marriott lists active hotels in Mexico City.[4][16]\n- **Four Seasons**, **Ritz-Carlton**, and **Fairmont**, all of which appear in Mexico’s luxury hotel landscape and are frequently used as benchmark brands by developers targeting higher-end positioning.[2][4]\n- **Hilton**, **Sofitel**, and **Mandarin Oriental**, which also show up in the Mexico luxury set and are commonly considered in upscale-to-luxury feasibility discussions.[4][6][7]\n- **Grand Velas**, **Hyatt Ziva**, **Zoëtry**, and **The Tides/Belmond-style luxury independent or soft brands** for resort-style upper-upscale and luxury projects, especially in beach destinations.[3][4][8][13]\n\nIf you want the **most likely shortlist for an owner aiming at a true upper-upscale, full-service hotel in Mexico City or a major secondary market**, the practical core group is usually **Camino Real, Fiesta Americana, JW Marriott, Hilton, Marriott, and Sofitel**, with **Four Seasons/Ritz-Carlton/Fairmont** as luxury comparables rather than pure upper-upscale targets.[1][3][4][6][11][16]\n\nIf helpful, I can turn this into a **brand shortlist by city** (Mexico City, Monterrey, Guadalajara, Cancún, Riviera Maya, Los Cabos) or into a **tiered matrix: upper-upscale vs. luxury vs. resort**.",
